      "title": "Testing Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Testing Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What TestClient Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`TestClient` (from `fastapi.testclient`) wraps your ==ASGI app==",
                "Calls it ==in-process==: no real server, no network port",
                "Built on **httpx**",
                "==Synchronous==: plain `def` test, no `await`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def test_items():",
                "    with TestClient(app) as client:",
                "        r = client.get('/items')",
                "        assert r.status_code == 200"
              ],
              "note": "no await needed"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "with TestClient(app)",
                "bare TestClient(app)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Startup/shutdown lifespan",
                  "{green:runs}",
                  "{red:skipped}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Test Pyramid for APIs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unit",
                    "note": "pure functions, many",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "note": "endpoints via TestClient",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Real network",
                    "note": "few",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Testing against a running ==uvicorn== server",
                "Using a real database in tests",
                "Result: tests are **slow** and **flaky**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Use `with TestClient(app) as client` or ==lifespan events never run==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "TestClient and AsyncClient Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TestClient and AsyncClient Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. TestClient basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def test_create(client):",
                "    r = client.post('/items', json={'name': 'x'})",
                "    assert r.status_code == 201",
                "    assert r.json()['name'] == 'x'"
              ],
              "note": "sync: plain def, no await"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. AsyncClient",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Needs ==transport=ASGITransport(app=app)== and `base_url='http://test'`",
                "The `app=` shortcut is {red:removed} in current httpx",
                "Async tests need ==pytest-asyncio== or the **anyio** marker"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import pytest",
                "from httpx import AsyncClient, ASGITransport",
                "",
                "@pytest.mark.anyio",
                "async def test_root():",
                "    t = ASGITransport(app=app)",
                "    async with AsyncClient(transport=t, base_url='http://test') as ac:",
                "        r = await ac.get('/')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "TestClient",
                "AsyncClient"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Test function",
                  "plain `def`",
                  "`async def`"
                ],
                [
                  "Choose when",
                  "nothing to await",
                  "test awaits (async DB, async fixtures)"
                ],
                [
                  "Lifespan",
                  "runs inside `with`",
                  "{red:not run}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ASGITransport ==skips lifespan== events: wrap with asgi-lifespan `LifespanManager` or run startup yourself",
                "No `@pytest.mark.anyio` / asyncio marker: the async test is **skipped** or errors out"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "TestClient by default; AsyncClient only when the test itself must ==await==, and then add the marker."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dependency Overrides and Fixtures",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dependency Overrides and Fixtures",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Overriding a dependency",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = fake_get_db` swaps a `Depends` callable",
                "The key is the ==function object==, not a string",
                "Override the callable the route uses, e.g. `get_current_user`, to skip auth"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "app.dependency_overrides[get_current_user] = lambda: User(id=1)",
                "r = client.get('/me')"
              ],
              "note": "no login needed in the test"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fixtures in conftest.py",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Always clear overrides after the test, or they ==leak== into other tests",
                "Test DB: session in a transaction or in-memory SQLite, override `get_db` to yield it, ==roll back== after",
                "Scope: {green:function} (default) isolates tests; {blue:session} speeds up setup like creating tables"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@pytest.fixture",
                "def client():",
                "    with TestClient(app) as c:",
                "        yield c",
                "    app.dependency_overrides.clear()"
              ],
              "note": "clear runs after the test, even on failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Override never matches",
              "text": "The route's `Depends` holds a different object (wrapped or re-created). The key must be the ==same object==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why clear overrides?** The app is global, so they leak into later tests.",
                "**What is the key?** The original function object.",
                "**Why roll back the DB?** Each test starts from clean data."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings with pydantic-settings",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Settings with pydantic-settings",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. BaseSettings",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Install separately: `pip install pydantic-settings`",
                "`class Settings(BaseSettings)`: typed fields read ==env vars== and `.env`",
                "Env names are **case-insensitive**; `env_prefix` adds `APP_`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from pydantic import SecretStr",
                "from pydantic_settings import BaseSettings, SettingsConfigDict",
                "class Settings(BaseSettings):",
                "    model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_file='.env', env_prefix='APP_')",
                "    db_url: str",
                "    api_key: SecretStr",
                "    debug: bool = False"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Precedence and failure",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Init args",
                    "sub": "wins",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Env vars",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".env file",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Defaults",
                    "sub": "last",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing required field → ==ValidationError== at startup (fail fast)",
                "`SecretStr` is masked in repr and logs; read with `.get_secret_value()`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. FastAPI wiring",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@lru_cache",
                "def get_settings(): return Settings()",
                "@app.get('/info')",
                "def info(s: Settings = Depends(get_settings)): ...",
                "# test",
                "app.dependency_overrides[get_settings] = lambda: Settings(db_url='sqlite://', api_key='x')"
              ],
              "note": "@lru_cache builds Settings once"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistakes",
              "text": "Committing `.env`, or reading `os.environ` directly: values stay **untyped** and unvalidated."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Uvicorn, Gunicorn and Docker",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Uvicorn, Gunicorn and Docker",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Running Uvicorn",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dev: ==--reload== gives one process with auto reload, **never** for production",
                "`--host 0.0.0.0` is needed inside containers",
                "`--workers N` starts several processes (or `fastapi run --workers 4`)",
                "{red:--reload and --workers cannot be combined}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "uvicorn app.main:app --reload",
                "uvicorn app.main:app --workers 4",
                "gunicorn app.main:app -k uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker -w 4 -b 0.0.0.0:8000"
              ],
              "note": "dev, Uvicorn workers, Gunicorn manager"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Workers and Gunicorn",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Gunicorn** is a process manager using ==UvicornWorker==",
                "Newer Uvicorn has its own supervisor, so Gunicorn is ==optional==",
                "Workers are **separate processes**, no shared memory",
                "Caches and globals differ per worker: use ==Redis or a DB== for shared state"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Docker and Deployment",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "FROM python:3.12-slim",
                "WORKDIR /app",
                "COPY requirements.txt .",
                "RUN pip install -r requirements.txt",
                "COPY . .",
                "CMD [\"uvicorn\",\"app.main:app\",\"--host\",\"0.0.0.0\",\"--port\",\"80\"]"
              ],
              "note": "requirements first = cached layer; exec-form CMD"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Where",
                "Processes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Kubernetes",
                  "**One** Uvicorn per container, scale with replicas"
                ],
                [
                  "Single VM",
                  "Workers near ==CPU core count=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistakes",
              "text": "Shell-form CMD: signals are not forwarded, graceful shutdown breaks. Binding `127.0.0.1`: the container port is unreachable."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
